      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Sometimes when VRChat is under load, I won't be able to see or hear other people (or they flicker in and out) and they won't be able to see or hear me. Even the nametags can disappear.\nIt usually happens when frame time is over 11 milliseconds in a detailed world (Vive runs at 90Hz), and I seem to have occasional success by dropping the render resolution in that case, but when I go to a world that isn't normally loaded and manually increase the render resolution, I can still see other avatars.\nThis is my third day running VRChat with a headset, so I haven't thoroughly tested this yet. I have tried checking download integrity from steam, clearing VRChat's cache, clearing Steam download cache, reinstalling VRChat, and upgrading my video card driver, but none helped.\nI'm going to check the logs tomorrow to see if there's also a deserialization issue.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
